Key Changes in RaftElectionService.java (TV5-D28 Freeze):
1. [NO_MOCK_IN_PRODUCTION] RuntimeMode (PRODUCTION | TEST_SIMULATION) & Fail-Closed Production Enforcement:
   - Added `RuntimeMode`, `RaftElectionService.production(...)` factories, `RaftElectionService.fromEnvironment(...)`, `resolveRuntimeMode(...)`, and `isProductionModeConfigured()`.
   - In `RuntimeMode.PRODUCTION`: requires non-null durable `RaftStorage`, `PersistentRaftNode` (rejects mock `RaftNode`), real `VoteTransport` (rejects null or `NO_OP_TRANSPORT`), and validated `TimeoutConfig`; auto-wires real `WriteAvailabilityPolicy` (`ReplicationTracker` + `CommitAdvancer`) upon LEADER promotion; rejects fallback mock quorum counting.
   - Blocks all simulation/mock methods in `PRODUCTION` mode with `UnsupportedOperationException` + WARNING log: `isolatePeer()`, `healPeer()`, `partition()`, `healAll()`, `simulateStopLeader()`, `simulateRestartAfterStop()`, `setClock()`, `clearTermLog()`.
   - Rejects the 4-argument no-transport test constructor when `RAFT_MODE` / `RAILWAY_MODE` / `railway.raft.mode` is set to `production`.
2. [COMPLETE_EVENT_LOGS] Structured Election & Recovery Event Logging:
   - Added lifecycle/safety event constants: `EVENT_NODE_STARTED`, `EVENT_TIMEOUT_CONFIGURED`, `EVENT_VOTE_DENIED`, `EVENT_STEP_DOWN`, `EVENT_RECOVERY_FAILED`, `EVENT_FAIL_CLOSED` (alongside D25 constants).
   - `recordTermEvent()` sets effective `leaderId` (`localId` when `Role.LEADER`), emits structured `[RAFT-ELECTION]` records to `java.util.logging.Logger` (INFO/WARNING/SEVERE) with `mode`, `lastApplied`, `commitIndex`, `lastLogIndex`, `term`, `role`, `leader`, `votedFor`, and notifies registered listeners (`addEventListener`/`removeEventListener`).
   - Records `VOTE_GRANTED` / `VOTE_DENIED` on incoming `VoteTransport` replies (preserving chronological order before synchronous `LEADER_ELECTED`), `handleRequestVote()` denials, `recordVoteResponse()` denials/ignores, same-term `STEP_DOWN`, `RECOVERY_FAILED`, and `FAIL_CLOSED` (including storage term regression in `validateDurableState()`).
   - Added `TermLogEntry.toDetailedLogLine(lastApplied, mode)` and `exportEventLogs()`.
3. [TIMEOUT_CONFIG] Validated Election & Quorum Timeout Configuration:
   - Added `TimeoutConfig(ElectionConfig electionConfig, Duration rpcTimeout, Duration quorumFreshnessWindow)` with `defaults()`, `lanProductionDefaults()`, `fromEnvironment(env, props)` (reads `RAFT_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS`, `RAFT_ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MIN_MS`, `RAFT_ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MAX_MS`, `RAFT_RPC_TIMEOUT_MS` / `TCP_RESPONSE_DEADLINE_MS`, `RAFT_QUORUM_FRESHNESS_MS`), and `validateForProduction()` enforcing `electionMin >= 3 * heartbeat`, `electionMax - electionMin >= heartbeat`, `rpcTimeout <= electionMax`, and `quorumFreshness >= 3 * heartbeat`.
   - Propagates `quorumFreshnessWindow` to `WriteAvailabilityPolicy` and `ElectionConfig` to `ElectionTimeoutPolicy` (`nextElectionTimeoutMillis()`).

